  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "aa32fd99-3d35-4259-a81f-b32345c1169a",
      "text": "Grabbiness is the fact that sudden changes in a perceived thing provoke an automatic orienting reflex, so changes in the thing immediately affect sensory stimulation, while changes in a thing merely thought about do not.",
